DECISION: phase_e1_stress3_gate_consistency_and_plateau_timing_analysis
VALUE:     LyASC_stress_3.0 (n=5 seeds) achieves two distinct outcome clusters observed in this sample: 1 seed Full Rescue (Seed 4: 8.75% test error, alpha=0.8285) vs 4 seeds Partial Rescue (Seeds 0-3: mean 25.16%, median 20.88%, range 19.12%-32.73%, alpha ~0.64-0.66). [Footnote: Pooled 5-seed mean is 21.88% ± 9.15pp vs paper baseline 49.27% [LN(x+3F)]]. Driven by a continuous threshold effect of early escape speed.
RATIONALE: Detailed empirical evaluation and config audit (MLflow & training logs):

1. Config Verification (Confirmed Fact):
   - Verified Seed 4 model instantiation: skip_scale=1.0, residual_scale=3.0, use_layer_norm=True genuinely applied across all 54 LyASCSkip blocks.
   - Initial gradient norm at iter 1000 was 1.185M (matching Seeds 0-3 at 1.15M-1.44M, ~5.6x unstressed baseline), confirming the 3x residual scaling pre-factor was active throughout training.

2. Unified Continuous Threshold Effect:
   - Escape speed before ~16k is the single governing variable determining outcome regime:
     * Full Rescue Breakthrough (Seed 4: 8.75% error): Early optimization progress before ~16k (alpha_mean passing 0.7060 at iter 16k, loss reaching 0.4081 at 27k) triggers full gate breakthrough to alpha = 0.8285, matching standard non-stressed baseline performance (8.75%).
     * Partial Rescue Regime (Seeds 0-3: 19.12%-32.73% error): Slower initial progress caps alpha_mean at ~0.64-0.66. Within this regime, plateau escape timing relative to the 32k LR drop determines final error (Seeds 2 & 3 escaping at 27k-28k reach 19.12% & 20.88%; Seeds 0 & 1 stalling/relapsing at 32k reach 27.90% & 32.73%).

3. Sample-Specific Cluster Breakdown (n=5 Seeds):
   - Full Rescue Cluster (1 seed in this sample): Seed 4 — 8.75% test error (alpha_mean = 0.8285).
   - Partial Rescue Cluster (4 seeds in this sample): Seeds 0, 1, 2, 3 — 25.16% mean error (median 20.88%, range 19.12% - 32.73%, alpha_mean ~0.64 - 0.66).
   - Sample Note: Described as observed in this sample (n=5); population frequency of full vs partial breakthrough requires larger sample sizes.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECISION: phase_e2_normalization_pairing_ablation_complete
VALUE:     Ground-truth LyASC+LN baseline confirmed as Phase D closed-out result: 7.17% ± 0.21% (seeds 7.33%, 7.25%, 6.93%). Reused without retraining. LyASC_noG (G=Identity) test error = 9.52% ± 0.98% (+2.35pp penalty vs LyASC+LN 7.17%); LyASC+BN (G=BatchNorm2d) test error = 6.34% ± 0.01% (observed difference of -0.83pp vs LyASC+LN 7.17%).
RATIONALE: Baseline Audit & Phase E2 normalization pairing ablations completed (depth 110, 64k iters, 2 seeds each):
1. Baseline Audit & Provenance Verification: Reused pre-registered Phase D cold-start 'none' baseline for LyASC+LN (3-seed mean: 7.17% ± 0.21%, seeds 0-2: 7.33%, 7.25%, 6.93%). No retraining performed. Provenance check confirmed draft table figures (6.31%, 6.32%, 6.39%) were pulled from base paper reference values; ground-truth 7.17% baseline restored.
2. LyASC_noG (G=Identity, no post-gate norm): Seed 0 = 10.21%, Seed 1 = 8.82% (2-seed mean: 9.52% ± 0.98%, alpha_mean = 0.6580). Omitting post-gate normalization incurs a +2.35pp penalty vs LyASC+LN (7.17%), confirming post-gate normalization is necessary.
3. LyASC+BN (G=BatchNorm2d): Seed 0 = 6.35%, Seed 1 = 6.33% (2-seed mean: 6.34% ± 0.01%, alpha_mean = 0.5621). In unstressed training, this represents an observed difference of -0.83pp vs LyASC+LN (7.17%, n=3). This result is statistically indistinguishable from plain 1xSkip (6.27%-6.36%) and remains above 2rSkip+LN (6.15%). The behavior of LyASC+BN under stress conditions remains untested.
------------------------------------------------------------------------


